d, since merging into main needs a code owner's approval.\n\n- **Cause:** `round_money` in `src/money.py` used the wrong rounding mode (`ROUND_HALF_UP`), even though its own description said banker's rounding. So `2.665` came out as `2.67` instead of the `2.66` the test expects.\n- **Fix:** On branch `fix/money-half-even-rounding`, I switched it to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`.\n- **CI:** Run ci-0001 passed on that change.\n- **PR:** https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101. The response to opening it listed no reviewers, so I added alex in a separate request, and that request confirmed him as reviewer.\n\nI couldn't look up FIN-212 because the advisory system returned \"Unknown advisory FIN-212\". The fix follows what the test and the code's own description say, and I mentioned the failed lookup in the PR description.", "type": "text"}]}]}